  "energy_arc": "Mukhada establishes regal melodic authority over heavy groove (6/10) -> Guitar takeover tightens the palm-muted chug and thickens the distortion (8/10) -> Sitar taan climax reaches maximum technical and dynamic peak (10/10) -> Returning mukhada locks into unison rhythm and hits a crushing hard stop on sam (9/10)",
  "rhythm_section": {
    "reasoning": "Plan: Ground the regal Darbari Kanada with a heavy metal foundation in key of E (S=E). Section 0 (Mukhada): Follow the harmony plan (S 8, g 4, R 2, S 2). In avartan 1 & 2, drive with palm-muted gallops and steady power chords on S(-1), shift to g(-1) over the sitar's ornamentation, resolve through R(-1) back to S(-1). Section 1 (takeover) is skipped per instructions as code arranges the guitar takeover from the realised head. Section 2 (taan_long): Hold driving pedal chugs on S(-1) power chords with steady 8ths and gallop figures to underpin the blazing 16th-note sitar runs without clashing harmonically. Section 3 (mukhada reprise): Uses same_as: 0 to bring back the original anthemic mukhada chord progression and hit the final sam stop.",
